# Build-context excludes for `docker build` (Dockerfile.build).
#
# Dockerfile.build installs a toolchain and COPYs nothing from the repo, so the
# build context is unused — but without this file Docker uploads the ENTIRE
# folder to the daemon, including src-tauri/target/ (tens to hundreds of GB of
# Rust build artifacts). Excluding the heavy, irrelevant paths keeps the context
# tiny and `docker build` fast.
.git/
node_modules/
dist/
dist-linux/
target-docker/
src-tauri/target/
src-tauri/binaries/
**/*.deb
**/*.AppImage
**/*.rpm
**/*.log
